1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,900
- What happened to Serizawa?
- He's sick.

2
00:00:01,900 --> 00:00:03,330
I want to meet him.

3
00:00:03,330 --> 00:00:04,790
Suzuki.

4
00:00:04,790 --> 00:00:06,960
You really came.

5
00:00:06,960 --> 00:00:10,710
You've never felt your heart beat faster

6
00:00:10,710 --> 00:00:12,750
when you're around Serizawa?

7
00:00:15,550 --> 00:00:18,250
<i>Maybe I...</i>

8
00:00:18,250 --> 00:00:19,940
Sorry, I'm going home!

9
00:00:19,940 --> 00:00:21,990
Don't go.

10
00:00:23,520 --> 00:00:25,950
<i>Maybe...</i>

11
00:00:27,250 --> 00:00:29,150
<i>I really do like Serizawa.</i>

12
00:01:16,560 --> 00:01:18,600
Serizawa?

13
00:01:21,440 --> 00:01:23,900
Wait!

14
00:01:44,310 --> 00:01:47,760
Can I kiss you?

15
00:01:47,760 --> 00:01:49,660
What are you...

16
00:01:50,610 --> 00:01:53,480
Suzuki.

17
00:01:53,480 --> 00:01:56,890
You like me, don't you?

18
00:02:03,800 --> 00:02:05,680
Hey, wait!

19
00:02:05,680 --> 00:02:07,470
No...

20
00:02:07,470 --> 00:02:09,080
Don't!

21
00:02:12,340 --> 00:02:15,420
A dream?

22
00:02:17,350 --> 00:02:21,550
For real? Oh no...

23
00:02:21,550 --> 00:02:25,040
My imagination is running wild...

24
00:02:26,880 --> 00:02:29,150
<i>Yesterday night...</i>

25
00:02:31,050 --> 00:02:35,500
<i>My heart was beating like crazy, so...</i>

26
00:02:42,740 --> 00:02:44,510
Sorry, change of plans.

27
00:02:44,510 --> 00:02:45,880
I'm going home.

28
00:02:45,880 --> 00:02:48,090
- Huh?
- I'm really sorry!

29
00:02:48,090 --> 00:02:50,730
Call or text if you need something.

30
00:02:50,730 --> 00:02:52,430
Take care!

31
00:02:57,360 --> 00:02:59,910
<i>Maybe...</i>

32
00:02:59,910 --> 00:03:04,540
<i>I do like Serizawa.</i>

33
00:03:09,110 --> 00:03:11,370
[Notification]

34
00:03:12,320 --> 00:03:15,290
<i>Morning, Suzuki! Thanks for coming yesterday.</i>

35
00:03:15,290 --> 00:03:18,270
<i>Your nursing put me right back in gear.</i>

36
00:03:23,050 --> 00:03:27,600
<i>And you felt great as a body pillow.</i>

37
00:03:28,510 --> 00:03:30,210
What?

38
00:03:31,100 --> 00:03:34,220
<i>I take back everything I thought earlier.</i>

39
00:03:34,220 --> 00:03:38,560
<i>I won't fall in love with Serizawa.</i>

40
00:03:38,560 --> 00:03:40,400
[Quit teasing me]

41
00:04:29,410 --> 00:04:34,180
[Episode 5]

42
00:04:35,470 --> 00:04:37,070
Morning.

43
00:04:37,070 --> 00:04:38,680
- Hey.
- 'Sup.

44
00:04:38,680 --> 00:04:40,420
What's going on?

45
00:04:40,420 --> 00:04:41,960
Well...

46
00:04:41,960 --> 00:04:46,050
Serizawa's being held prisoner.

47
00:04:46,050 --> 00:04:47,350
By who?

48
00:04:47,350 --> 00:04:49,060
Some third year upperclassmen.

49
00:04:49,060 --> 00:04:50,500
Take a look.

50
00:04:52,630 --> 00:04:54,110
- Why not?
- Sorry.

51
00:04:54,110 --> 00:04:57,170
I made plans to play ball with the boys.

52
00:04:57,170 --> 00:04:59,960
- Let us join you!
- Or ditch them!

53
00:04:59,960 --> 00:05:02,200
Did Serizawa get on their bad side?

54
00:05:02,200 --> 00:05:05,970
Far from it.

55
00:05:06,880 --> 00:05:08,360
A date?

56
00:05:08,360 --> 00:05:11,630
Remember those snacks we had the other day?

57
00:05:11,630 --> 00:05:14,380
Snacks...

58
00:05:15,570 --> 00:05:17,660
<i>Koha got them from her upperclassmen.</i>

59
00:05:17,660 --> 00:05:19,220
<i>For real? Sweet!</i>

60
00:05:19,220 --> 00:05:21,410
- Right.
- Yeah, well those snacks

61
00:05:21,410 --> 00:05:24,070
were a trap.

62
00:05:24,070 --> 00:05:25,210
A trap?

63
00:05:25,210 --> 00:05:27,240
They asked Serizawa out on a date

64
00:05:27,240 --> 00:05:30,220
in exchange for those snacks.

65
00:05:30,220 --> 00:05:31,390
Huh?

66
00:05:31,390 --> 00:05:33,500
It's not a date.

67
00:05:33,500 --> 00:05:37,120
One of the girls just wants to hang out

68
00:05:37,120 --> 00:05:39,840
and chat for an hour after school.

69
00:05:39,840 --> 00:05:42,550
We call that a date.

70
00:05:43,530 --> 00:05:45,720
If you're not up for it, tell her no.

71
00:05:45,720 --> 00:05:47,450
I did.

72
00:05:47,450 --> 00:05:50,610
But her friends pressured me like crazy.

73
00:05:50,610 --> 00:05:52,780
They insisted it'd only be the one time.

74
00:05:52,780 --> 00:05:56,290
Dude, why are you so upset? It's a date.

75
00:05:56,290 --> 00:05:58,490
If anything,

76
00:05:58,490 --> 00:06:01,060
you could take her as your girlfriend.

77
00:06:01,970 --> 00:06:06,900
I'm not really a fan of dating for fun.

78
00:06:07,940 --> 00:06:13,130
I don't want to hurt my partners,

79
00:06:13,130 --> 00:06:15,810
knowing my heart's not in it 100%.

80
00:06:19,180 --> 00:06:24,260
That's why all your relationships
have failed.

81
00:06:29,850 --> 00:06:33,240
Suzuki, did I disappoint?

82
00:06:33,240 --> 00:06:35,400
No, not at all.

83
00:06:35,400 --> 00:06:42,000
So, does that mean you...

84
00:06:43,490 --> 00:06:45,430
Uh...

85
00:06:45,430 --> 00:06:47,710
You don't have a girlfriend now?

86
00:06:47,710 --> 00:06:49,820
- Yeah.
- You just realized?

87
00:06:49,820 --> 00:06:51,450
Sorry.

88
00:06:51,450 --> 00:06:55,000
I didn't know.

89
00:06:55,800 --> 00:06:57,630
I'm single.

90
00:06:57,630 --> 00:07:02,030
Have been for over a year now.

91
00:07:04,550 --> 00:07:06,400
I see.

92
00:07:06,400 --> 00:07:08,600
That's unexpected.

93
00:07:08,600 --> 00:07:10,680
I'm the only taken dude here.

94
00:07:10,680 --> 00:07:12,510
Wait, really?

95
00:07:13,600 --> 00:07:16,660
Yeah. I'm not looking to date right now.

96
00:07:16,660 --> 00:07:21,100
And I don't need a girlfriend.

97
00:07:21,100 --> 00:07:23,510
Yeah, 'cause you prefer playing around.

98
00:07:23,510 --> 00:07:25,220
- Ouch.
- I see.

99
00:07:25,220 --> 00:07:26,780
My bad.

100
00:07:27,620 --> 00:07:29,510
What about you, Suzuki?

101
00:07:31,260 --> 00:07:32,810
Me?

102
00:07:33,850 --> 00:07:36,830
I don't have anyone like that.

103
00:07:36,830 --> 00:07:39,750
Romance is far beyond me anyway.

104
00:07:39,750 --> 00:07:42,180
You've never dated anyone?

105
00:07:44,890 --> 00:07:46,390
Nope.

106
00:07:48,870 --> 00:07:50,650
I see.

107
00:07:52,050 --> 00:07:54,870
So, when's your date

108
00:07:54,870 --> 00:07:58,090
with the upperclassman?

109
00:07:58,090 --> 00:08:01,450
We haven't decided. And it's not a date!

110
00:08:01,450 --> 00:08:03,480
Who knows? Maybe you two will get along.

111
00:08:03,480 --> 00:08:05,830
- It's a date!
- It's not!

112
00:08:05,830 --> 00:08:08,880
A date! A date!

113
00:08:08,880 --> 00:08:11,370
A date! A date!

114
00:08:11,370 --> 00:08:12,800
[Date]

115
00:08:12,800 --> 00:08:14,600
<i>A date.</i>

116
00:08:16,300 --> 00:08:17,780
<i>Right.</i>

117
00:08:19,170 --> 00:08:24,350
<i>I'm sure the girls must love Serizawa.</i>

118
00:08:25,990 --> 00:08:29,600
<i>They'd get into the mood,</i>

119
00:08:29,600 --> 00:08:32,260
<i>feel that special pull,</i>

120
00:08:34,210 --> 00:08:37,780
<i>and maybe start dating right then and there?</i>

121
00:08:42,860 --> 00:08:44,750
Suzuki.

122
00:08:46,500 --> 00:08:48,340
Serizawa.

123
00:08:48,340 --> 00:08:51,050
I knew I'd find you here.

124
00:08:51,050 --> 00:08:53,110
Were you writing?

125
00:08:53,110 --> 00:08:54,690
Yeah.

126
00:08:59,230 --> 00:09:01,060
Everything okay?

127
00:09:01,060 --> 00:09:03,160
Huh? Why?

128
00:09:03,160 --> 00:09:06,120
You look a bit down.

129
00:09:06,120 --> 00:09:08,180
Is something on your mind?

130
00:09:12,030 --> 00:09:13,500
Huh?

131
00:09:14,550 --> 00:09:16,750
"Date"?

132
00:09:17,660 --> 00:09:19,600
No, this was...

133
00:09:19,600 --> 00:09:22,100
Oh, I get it.

134
00:09:22,100 --> 00:09:24,770
Are you trying to write a date scene?

135
00:09:26,860 --> 00:09:28,540
Y-Yeah.

136
00:09:28,540 --> 00:09:32,350
I have no experience in that field,

137
00:09:32,350 --> 00:09:34,640
so I hit a bit of a wall.

138
00:09:35,820 --> 00:09:40,350
You should have told me!

139
00:09:40,350 --> 00:09:44,420
I said I'd help you out, right?

140
00:09:45,690 --> 00:09:47,480
Thanks.

141
00:09:53,380 --> 00:09:57,360
But I'll figure this one out myself.

142
00:10:04,190 --> 00:10:07,870
Want to give it a try, with me?

143
00:10:07,870 --> 00:10:10,700
Give what a try?

144
00:10:12,560 --> 00:10:14,250
A date.

145
00:10:22,300 --> 00:10:24,990
<i>I actually said yes.</i>

146
00:10:26,210 --> 00:10:30,230
<i>Me and Serizawa, on a date?</i>

147
00:10:30,230 --> 00:10:32,300
<i>Nope. No way.</i>

148
00:10:32,300 --> 00:10:35,760
<i>Jeez, I hope I don't look weird.</i>

149
00:10:35,760 --> 00:10:39,280
Maybe I should've bought a new outfit.

150
00:10:39,280 --> 00:10:43,240
Not that I even have one fashionable fit.

151
00:10:44,850 --> 00:10:46,510
Suzuki.

152
00:11:01,250 --> 00:11:07,630
<i>His casual clothes are blinding!</i>

153
00:11:09,560 --> 00:11:12,190
Sorry, did I keep you waiting?

154
00:11:15,610 --> 00:11:17,410
Never mind.

155
00:11:18,490 --> 00:11:21,600
- Not happening.
- Where are you going?

156
00:11:22,680 --> 00:11:25,770
Sorry, it's just...

157
00:11:25,770 --> 00:11:29,130
You look too cool.

158
00:11:29,130 --> 00:11:31,000
Aw, thanks for the compliment.

159
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:33,120
Of course I'd dress my best today.

160
00:11:33,120 --> 00:11:35,550
I've got a date with you.

161
00:11:35,550 --> 00:11:36,780
A date...

162
00:11:36,780 --> 00:11:38,710
Come on, let's go.

163
00:11:38,710 --> 00:11:39,850
Where?

164
00:11:39,850 --> 00:11:42,400
Somewhere I know you'll love.

165
00:11:52,530 --> 00:11:54,970
No way...

166
00:11:54,970 --> 00:11:59,700
This is where HaseFuka had their first date
in "Stars in the Deep Sea"!

167
00:11:59,700 --> 00:12:01,810
Why?

168
00:12:01,810 --> 00:12:05,190
Why not do a drama pilgrimage on our date?

169
00:12:05,190 --> 00:12:08,260
You're the best, Serizawa.

170
00:12:08,260 --> 00:12:10,920
This is amazing!

171
00:12:11,820 --> 00:12:13,880
I wish I brought my acrylic standees...

172
00:12:13,880 --> 00:12:17,390
I thought you'd say that.

173
00:12:18,720 --> 00:12:20,180
HaseFuka standees?

174
00:12:20,180 --> 00:12:22,060
Genius.

175
00:12:22,060 --> 00:12:24,420
You're too perfect.

176
00:12:24,420 --> 00:12:25,710
Right?

177
00:12:25,710 --> 00:12:27,170
Here.

178
00:12:28,270 --> 00:12:30,320
Hasegawa...

179
00:12:31,370 --> 00:12:32,700
Right, pictures.

180
00:12:32,700 --> 00:12:34,870
Let's take plenty.

181
00:12:34,870 --> 00:12:36,420
Ready?

182
00:12:36,420 --> 00:12:38,880
Say cheese.

183
00:12:42,600 --> 00:12:43,650
Another one?

184
00:12:43,650 --> 00:12:45,500
Sounds good.

185
00:12:46,970 --> 00:12:50,310
Say cheese.

186
00:12:56,800 --> 00:12:58,370
There are so many fish.

187
00:12:58,370 --> 00:13:00,370
You're right.

188
00:13:00,370 --> 00:13:02,110
I think those are char.

189
00:13:02,110 --> 00:13:03,830
- Char?
- Yeah.

190
00:13:09,940 --> 00:13:12,880
Know what scene happens here?

191
00:13:12,880 --> 00:13:14,790
Isn't this where HaseFuka held hands?

192
00:13:14,790 --> 00:13:16,290
Bingo.

193
00:13:16,290 --> 00:13:18,220
Here.

194
00:13:18,220 --> 00:13:19,460
Huh?

195
00:13:19,460 --> 00:13:21,350
This is a date, isn't it?

196
00:13:22,260 --> 00:13:25,470
But we're only doing it for research.

197
00:13:25,470 --> 00:13:26,730
Exactly.

198
00:13:26,730 --> 00:13:30,810
So, let's really go through
the motions of a date.

199
00:13:36,120 --> 00:13:39,310
Not like that. Like this.

200
00:13:41,990 --> 00:13:44,290
Come on.

201
00:13:44,290 --> 00:13:46,090
<i>Woah.</i>

202
00:13:46,920 --> 00:13:49,340
<i>My heart's pounding...</i>

203
00:13:49,340 --> 00:13:50,700
Cute!

204
00:13:50,700 --> 00:13:52,290
There's a whole school in there.

205
00:13:52,290 --> 00:13:53,710
What's this fish called?

206
00:13:53,710 --> 00:13:56,740
- A piranha.
- That's definitely wrong.

207
00:13:57,600 --> 00:13:59,350
They're so cute...

208
00:13:59,350 --> 00:14:00,610
Small, too.

209
00:14:00,610 --> 00:14:02,260
Agreed.

210
00:14:02,260 --> 00:14:04,760
There's a smaller one over there!

211
00:14:04,760 --> 00:14:06,800
I've heard about these.

212
00:14:06,800 --> 00:14:08,470
Can I give it a try?

213
00:14:08,470 --> 00:14:11,980
Sure. Stick your hand in.

214
00:14:11,980 --> 00:14:13,290
Am I allowed to?

215
00:14:13,290 --> 00:14:14,930
Yeah. Go for it.

216
00:14:14,930 --> 00:14:16,890
They're already crowding!

217
00:14:16,890 --> 00:14:19,590
Wait, pause!

218
00:14:19,590 --> 00:14:22,130
There are way too many of them!

219
00:14:22,130 --> 00:14:26,670
Does this mean...

220
00:14:26,670 --> 00:14:28,600
Guess you had tons of dead skin built up.

221
00:14:28,600 --> 00:14:31,470
That's embarrassing.

222
00:14:31,470 --> 00:14:32,880
I feel exposed...

223
00:14:32,880 --> 00:14:35,570
- Let me see your hand.
- Okay.

224
00:14:46,790 --> 00:14:48,440
A capybara!

225
00:14:48,440 --> 00:14:50,810
Oh yeah, I see its face.

226
00:14:50,810 --> 00:14:53,080
It's poking its nose out.

227
00:14:53,080 --> 00:14:55,610
There's a turtle, too!

228
00:14:55,610 --> 00:14:57,090
I see it.

229
00:14:57,090 --> 00:14:59,200
Cute.

230
00:15:06,250 --> 00:15:08,720
HaseFuka rang this bell.

231
00:15:10,310 --> 00:15:13,210
Let's give it a try, too.

232
00:15:16,520 --> 00:15:18,490
Ready?

233
00:15:21,900 --> 00:15:23,120
Louder than I thought.

234
00:15:23,120 --> 00:15:25,620
- There's so much.
- I'd like to get something.

235
00:15:25,620 --> 00:15:27,480
Me too.

236
00:15:29,320 --> 00:15:31,520
That's cute.

237
00:15:31,520 --> 00:15:33,840
Let's buy a matching pair.

238
00:15:34,900 --> 00:15:41,490
<i>We're acting like a real couple.</i>

239
00:15:44,000 --> 00:15:45,910
Here you are.

240
00:15:45,910 --> 00:15:48,340
Enjoy your drinks!

241
00:15:54,700 --> 00:15:56,600
Isn't that guy good-looking?

242
00:15:56,600 --> 00:15:58,510
You're right. Maybe he's a model.

243
00:15:58,510 --> 00:15:59,650
Go ask him.

244
00:15:59,650 --> 00:16:02,890
No way! I'm not pretty enough
to be seen with him.

245
00:16:02,890 --> 00:16:05,080
Girl, you're too self-conscious.

246
00:16:09,250 --> 00:16:11,390
Hey, I'm back.

247
00:16:11,390 --> 00:16:15,420
Do you want the Blue Hawaiian
or the Cream Soda?

248
00:16:15,420 --> 00:16:17,170
Thanks.

249
00:16:18,030 --> 00:16:19,790
I'm fine with either.

250
00:16:20,840 --> 00:16:23,150
Then here.

251
00:16:27,990 --> 00:16:31,500
That's good. Try it.

252
00:16:31,500 --> 00:16:33,050
Sure.

253
00:16:45,860 --> 00:16:47,310
Thanks.

254
00:16:47,310 --> 00:16:49,050
It tastes good.

255
00:16:51,350 --> 00:16:52,950
Is everything okay?

256
00:16:52,950 --> 00:16:54,380
Fine.

257
00:16:55,450 --> 00:16:58,310
I just feel bad.

258
00:16:58,310 --> 00:17:00,210
Huh?

259
00:17:00,210 --> 00:17:05,110
I mean, I'm no match for you.

260
00:17:06,140 --> 00:17:07,510
What?

261
00:17:07,510 --> 00:17:09,040
I don't think I'm following.

262
00:17:09,040 --> 00:17:11,320
Don't you get it?

263
00:17:12,130 --> 00:17:16,650
You're good-looking,

264
00:17:16,650 --> 00:17:18,600
and you know how to dress yourself.

265
00:17:19,790 --> 00:17:24,290
But me?

266
00:17:24,290 --> 00:17:28,600
I'm so unstylish, I'm doing you a disservice.

267
00:17:28,600 --> 00:17:32,640
You're not giving yourself enough credit.

268
00:17:32,640 --> 00:17:34,040
Huh?

269
00:17:34,990 --> 00:17:39,900
Who cares about what others think?
I like your style.

270
00:17:39,900 --> 00:17:43,270
I like the outfit and your hair.

271
00:17:43,270 --> 00:17:45,710
I like your face and personality, too.

272
00:17:46,410 --> 00:17:49,610
You're being a bit too generous there.

273
00:17:49,610 --> 00:17:53,720
I also like how you're a dedicated writer.

274
00:17:53,720 --> 00:17:58,760
See? Even now, you're taking notes.

275
00:17:59,740 --> 00:18:05,560
But I've never finished a single story.

276
00:18:05,560 --> 00:18:12,010
I only take notes because
I have a bad memory, too.

277
00:18:13,740 --> 00:18:19,130
I'm not smart, nor athletic.

278
00:18:19,130 --> 00:18:25,280
It takes me double the time to accomplish
what others can do easily.

279
00:18:30,990 --> 00:18:33,550
Suzuki.

280
00:18:33,550 --> 00:18:36,410
Don't focus on the expectations of others.

281
00:18:36,410 --> 00:18:41,920
Accept the fact that I think you're awesome.

282
00:18:46,180 --> 00:18:49,040
You're adorable, Suzuki.

283
00:18:49,040 --> 00:18:52,800
You're at the top of my list
of people I want at my side.

284
00:18:58,150 --> 00:18:59,840
Got it?

285
00:19:01,330 --> 00:19:03,230
All right, good boy.

286
00:19:03,230 --> 00:19:05,880
Let me go.

287
00:19:07,070 --> 00:19:10,560
Stop it!

288
00:19:14,810 --> 00:19:16,850
So?

289
00:19:16,850 --> 00:19:20,830
Think you can write a date scene now?

290
00:19:20,830 --> 00:19:26,150
Yeah. Thanks for helping me out today.

291
00:19:29,880 --> 00:19:33,590
Huh? Isn't this...

292
00:19:33,590 --> 00:19:35,370
You finally noticed.

293
00:19:35,370 --> 00:19:38,030
I knew it. This is where HaseFuka kiss!

294
00:19:38,030 --> 00:19:39,970
Bingo.

295
00:19:41,550 --> 00:19:43,680
Wow...

296
00:19:51,410 --> 00:19:55,530
Are you going to write a kiss scene?

297
00:19:57,930 --> 00:20:02,010
Yeah. I plan to close out the date with one.

298
00:20:02,010 --> 00:20:05,930
I see. How will it play out?

299
00:20:05,930 --> 00:20:09,370
Uh, well...

300
00:20:09,370 --> 00:20:15,050
I think I'll have the top
stop the bottom from going home

301
00:20:15,050 --> 00:20:17,300
by asking for a kiss.

302
00:20:17,300 --> 00:20:19,230
And then...

303
00:20:19,980 --> 00:20:22,350
That's not bad.

304
00:20:22,350 --> 00:20:26,720
But how about something more natural?

305
00:20:27,370 --> 00:20:29,450
"Natural"?

306
00:20:33,510 --> 00:20:35,430
Face me.

307
00:20:42,020 --> 00:20:46,650
First, they'll happen to glance
at each other.

308
00:20:47,540 --> 00:20:53,080
Then, they'll gaze into each other's eyes.

309
00:20:53,080 --> 00:20:56,890
Slowly, but surely,

310
00:20:56,890 --> 00:21:01,300
their hearts will become one.

311
00:21:02,760 --> 00:21:08,850
And then, before they realize
what's happening...

312
00:21:37,350 --> 00:21:40,630
So? Did you get all that?

313
00:21:46,550 --> 00:21:48,400
Suzuki?

314
00:21:51,480 --> 00:21:53,750
<i>Oh no.</i>

315
00:21:53,750 --> 00:21:57,340
<i>I can't take this anymore.</i>

316
00:22:03,180 --> 00:22:07,190
Suzuki. Look at me.

317
00:22:22,640 --> 00:22:25,110
<i>I guess it's true.</i>

318
00:22:27,140 --> 00:22:29,660
<i>I...</i>

319
00:22:56,500 --> 00:22:58,330
<i>I like Serizawa after all.</i>

320
00:22:59,990 --> 00:23:04,590
Forget it, forget it, forget it.

321
00:23:04,590 --> 00:23:05,900
Forget it!

322
00:23:05,900 --> 00:23:08,340
- Wh-What?
- Nothing.

323
00:23:08,340 --> 00:23:11,300
Just wanted to say I had fun yesterday.

324
00:23:11,300 --> 00:23:15,000
As if I could forget.

